Of course, this is a very simple application of the concepts of vectors and projection. we know that projection, denoted with $proj_{\mathbf{w}}\mathbf{v}$ is defined as $proj_{\mathbf{w}}\mathbf{v} = \frac{\mathbf{v}\cdot\mathbf{w}}{\mathbf{w}\cdot\mathbf{w}}\mathbf{w}~$ Now, and using the facts that $\frac{|\mathbf{v}_{proj_{\mathbf{w}}\mathbf{v}}|}{|\mathbf{v}|}= \frac{5}{7}$ , or that $\frac{\mathbf{v}_{proj_{\mathbf{w}}\mathbf{v}}}{|\mathbf{v}|}= \frac{5}{7}$. Using that $\mathbf{p} = proj_{\mathbf{w}}\mathbf{v}$ ... 

The conversation continues up to the answer. The solution is as follows.
First, decompose $\mathbf{v}$ into two vectors. Notice that:
\begin{equation*}
\mathbf{v} = \mathbf{p} + (\mathbf{v} - \mathbf{p}).
\end{equation*}
Now consider $(\mathbf{v} - \mathbf{p})$. By definition of $\mathbf{p}$, it is the vector projection of $\mathbf{v}$ onto a vector orthogonal to $\mathbf{w}$. In terms of magnitudes, you can easily convince yourself that:
\begin{equation*}
\frac{\|\mathbf{v} - \mathbf{p}\|}{\|\mathbf{v}\|} = \sqrt{1 - \frac{25}{49} - \frac{25}{49}} = \frac{\sqrt{21}}{7}.
\end{equation*}
Notice $\frac{\|\mathbf{v} - \mathbf{p}\|}{\|\mathbf{v}\|} = \frac{\|\mathbf{v} - \mathbf{p}\|/|\mathbf{v}|}{\|\mathbf{v}\|/|\mathbf{v}|} = \frac{\|\mathbf{q}\|/|\mathbf{v}|}{1} = \frac{\|\mathbf{q}\|}{\|\mathbf{v}\|}.~$ Thus:
\begin{equation*}
\frac{\|\mathbf{q}\|}{\|\mathbf{v}\|} = \frac{\sqrt{21}}{7}.
\end{equation*}
Therefore, the answer is $\frac{\sqrt{21}}{7}$.

